WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:33.520
If there is one thing, that One Piece is known&nbsp;
for from a storytelling perspective, it’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:39.840
tragic &amp; powerful backstories of each single&nbsp;
straw hat, that are usually accompanied by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:47.040
tragic death of a loved one. And while the main&nbsp;
story line itself rarely leaves the adventurous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:54.160
spirit of a typical Shounen story, the flashbacks&nbsp;
are usually the places where Eiichiro Oda allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:00.320
himself to integrate deeper, darker and more&nbsp;
dramatic aspects of storytelling to add to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:06.400
epic world building, that might be considered as&nbsp;
too brutal for a week-to-week reading experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.520
So I think I don’t have to explain to you how&nbsp;
essential these scenes are to the overall appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:20.560
of a long-lasting story like One Piece. But I’ll&nbsp;
do it anyway. By showing us the tragic pasts that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.760
each of the diverse crew members have lived&nbsp;
through, Oda reveals that no matter who you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.360
are or where you come from, this world&nbsp;
and society is fundamentally broken.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:46.080
A world that allows for so much suffering, cruelty&nbsp;
and hardship cannot be allowed to continue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.920
and we need someone to change it. Say,&nbsp;
a rubber boy with a crew of dreamers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.600
And so, while there certainly are flashbacks&nbsp;
for other characters in the story as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:05.520
the general structure &amp; length of the straw hat&nbsp;
ones are exclusive to them. With one notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.880
exception. Law’s flashback on Dressrosa, which&nbsp;
stretches over 7 chapters, and which in my opinion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:19.040
is not only the key scene to unlock the entire&nbsp;
Dressrosa arc, but one of the most well-written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:25.360
and structured sequences in the story. And so&nbsp;
in today’s video, I want to look at Law’s and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.600
Corazon’s flashback, and why it is my favourite&nbsp;
piece of writing in the new world so far. Oh, yeah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.760
and if you haven’t done so already, make sure to&nbsp;
subscribe to the channel. No excuses. It’s free.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.120
The flashback takes place right&nbsp;
before the major battle between Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:56.160
and Doflamingo. When Law is facing off with Trebol&nbsp;
and Dofi, we finally get an insight into why Law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:02.400
feels so strongly about the warlord and why his&nbsp;
true objective had been Doflamingo all along.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.400
The young Law is found by some of the Doflamingo&nbsp;
family members after escaping his country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.400
As we will learn, Law is from a country called&nbsp;
Flevance, that got wealthy on a valuable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.720
but toxic material called Amber Lead, that&nbsp;
shortens the life span of each generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:27.280
drastically by accumulating in the body. Since&nbsp;
there is no cure for the toxic effect, Law as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:34.560
the son of doctors knows that he won’t even reach&nbsp;
his teens before dying a slow and painful death.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.240
As if this wasn’t tragic enough however, we&nbsp;
learn that the world government, as well as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:47.360
country’s nobles, knew right from the start about&nbsp;
the true danger of extracting the Lead, however&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:53.520
decided to keep it a secret to further enrich&nbsp;
themselves at the cost of the people’s lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:00.160
When the inhabitants of Flevence finally tried&nbsp;
to look for help in the neighbouring countries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:06.480
they were attacked and denied entry out of fear&nbsp;
of contagion. In a last attempt to get help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.040
the people took up arms, which gave the&nbsp;
other kingdoms the necessary justification&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.520
to invade and kill every single citizen, including&nbsp;
the orphan kids that Law had lived with after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.040
death of his parents. Seeing them shot in the&nbsp;
street as the hospital his sister was lying in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:30.400
went up in flames, pulled the young Law into deep&nbsp;
darkness. Severely traumatised, just as the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:43.840
Doflamingo, he turned his despair into feelings&nbsp;
of hatred and revenge. As a result, he joins the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:51.440
Doflamingo family with the goal to kill as many&nbsp;
people as possible before dying of his poisoning.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.560
The first time Law and we readers meet Corazon,&nbsp;
he is introduced as Dofi’s mute and clumsy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:06.240
younger brother who absolutely hates kids. Without&nbsp;
hesitation he grabs law and throws him out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:13.520
window. As we will later learn, Corazon did so in&nbsp;
the hope of pushing Law away from Dofi. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:20.800
quite understandably, it made Law hate loath&nbsp;
Corazon, whom he ultimately stabbed with a knife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.920
Knowing fully well, that Dofi would&nbsp;
kill him for attacking his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:32.000
he is surprised to find out that Corazon&nbsp;
has not sold him out. The real turn in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.920
their relationship however happens when Law&nbsp;
reveals his true name to Buffalo and Baby 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:51.680
Upon hearing Law’s secret middle name, Corazon&nbsp;
reveals his true self to Law and urges him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:58.720
get as far away from Dofi as possible. Law&nbsp;
declines, but also decides not to sell out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:07.040
Corazon in return. Already caring deeply for Law,&nbsp;
Corazon kidnapps him away from the family and goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:20.080
on a journey to find a cure for his illness,&nbsp;
during which the two grow closer and closer.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:26.560
Finally, when Law’s condition has worsened to a&nbsp;
worrying degree. They get intel from Doflamingo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:31.920
that they know the location of the OP OP&nbsp;
no Mi, the so-called ultimate devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:38.640
capable of switching personalities and matter,&nbsp;
as well as bestowing eternal life on another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.960
at the cost of the user’s own life. Doflamingo&nbsp;
wants this fruit above anything else to have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:51.600
immortality surgery performed on himself. Corazon&nbsp;
on the other hand wants to use it to save Law’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:58.240
life and at the same time get it out of Dofi’s&nbsp;
reach. So he contacts Sengoku to tip off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:04.800
Marines and takes Law to retain the fruit himself.&nbsp;
Despite getting heavily injured in the process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:10.880
he manages to claim the fruit and feed it&nbsp;
to Law. Trying to get help from the Marines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:18.320
he accidentally gives Corazon’s message to none&nbsp;
other than Vergo, Doflamingo’s spy in the marines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:24.480
who immeaditley notifies his boss and beats&nbsp;
Corazon half to death. When Dofi is on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:30.160
way to finish the job, Crazon hides Law in one&nbsp;
of the treasure chests and uses his powers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:37.360
mute the sound from within. Then he is confronted&nbsp;
and ultametly killed by his brother. Holding on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:44.720
to life to not give away Law’s cries, he finally&nbsp;
dies lying in the snow with a smile on his face.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:08:00.320
One thing this scene does incredibly well is give&nbsp;
deep characterisation for both law and Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:06.640
while introducing Corazon completely from scratch&nbsp;
in such a well-written way, that he ended up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:13.040
as one of my favourite characters in the show. I&nbsp;
already talked about Corazon’s fantastic character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:18.160
in a separate video, that I’ll link at the end of&nbsp;
this one. What I want to focus on in this video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:24.560
instead, is how this scene is constructed&nbsp;
and what makes it one of the most powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:30.960
moments in the story. And I think the secret&nbsp;
here is that Oda has basically built upon all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:36.640
his previous experience in the story, to create&nbsp;
the perfect flashback for a quasi-straw hat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:43.760
As a result, Law basically being an honorary&nbsp;
member of the crew at this point has the luck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:53.840
of getting a back story that builds on only the&nbsp;
best elements of previous straw hat stories.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.160
The first clear parallel I see is with&nbsp;
Chopper. The last part of Law’s story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:08.080
takes place on a quiet winter island that&nbsp;
gives the entire scene a unique ambient feel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:16.000
In storytelling snow mostly conveys at least&nbsp;
one of two emotions: Serenity and peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.840
as well as a slow creeping death in the cold.&nbsp;
In this case I would say it works as both.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:29.280
Both Corazon, as well as Hiruluk have a quite&nbsp;
quirky nature and both are shown to be conmen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:34.960
pretending to be something that they are not. But&nbsp;
while they appear to be rough and dishonest on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:42.160
outside, in the end both turn out to be two of of&nbsp;
the most kind and loving characters in the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:49.280
Just as doctor Hiruluk does for Chopper, Corazon&nbsp;
also gladly sacrifices himself for the good of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:55.120
someone else. Both characters have a medical&nbsp;
theme that is focused on both curing the body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:01.600
as well as curing the heart, both of whom manage&nbsp;
to do in the end, saving both Chopper and Law from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:09.760
their darkness as well as saving their lives. In&nbsp;
the end they die with a smile while the snow is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:24.000
falling. You could even compare Dr. Kureha and&nbsp;
Sengoku as forces sympathetic to their cause,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.800
that in the end are unable to really do&nbsp;
anything for them and have to mourn their death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:35.280
And of course both Chopper and Law end up becoming&nbsp;
doctors and pirates that end up traveling with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:41.760
Luffy. And finally, the big theme of inherited&nbsp;
will that is introduced to us on Drum Island is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:49.760
strongly repeated with Corazon. He sends Law on&nbsp;
his mission to find out more about the will of D.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:56.640
Another flashback we draw from is Nami. Just&nbsp;
as Nami grew up as a member of a ruthless and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:04.080
immoral pirate, Law did the same thing. Both Nami&nbsp;
and Law were fuelled by their anger and injustice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:11.280
In other ways, we also have some Sanji in there,&nbsp;
as Law goes from the toxic and hateful environment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:17.040
of the Doflamingo family to traveling with&nbsp;
Corazon, just as Sanji broke away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:32.240
Vinsmoke family to live and be raised by Jeff.
However the second big parallel, next to Chopper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:38.320
is with with Robin and her backstory. This is&nbsp;
actually interesting, because I would say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:45.200
Law and Robin are actually pretty much of the same&nbsp;
wavelength personality wise. Both of them are calm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:51.360
and have a dark aura around them, but also have&nbsp;
a nerdy and funny side that shows more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:57.680
as they travel with Luffy. Also, both of them&nbsp;
are scientists and both have a good grasp on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:04.080
politics of the world. And this reflects really&nbsp;
well in their flashbacks. Because as children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:09.840
both Robin and Law were quite cheerful kids,&nbsp;
until they were separated from their parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:14.320
Both had to witness the full&nbsp;
cruelty of the world government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.999
as they were responsible for the death of&nbsp;
their people. Both managed to flee the doom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.999 --> 00:12:18.320
of their loved ones as the sole survivor&nbsp;
of their respective kingdoms. And both were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.840
treated as outcasts and as dangerous by&nbsp;
the people of the world for their origin.

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:29.760
Both Robin’s and Choppers flashbacks are two&nbsp;
of my all-time favourite scenes in the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:35.280
And Oda took these wonderful elements out of&nbsp;
both of their back stories, as well as some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:39.920
minor successful elements from other straw&nbsp;
hats, to write the best flashback in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:46.400
story so far. This, combined with the fantastic&nbsp;
character design for both Corazon and Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:52.240
made for one of the most emotional moments&nbsp;
in the story, that at the same time served as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:57.760
the centre piece for the entire Dressrosa arc&nbsp;
and thus as a hefty piece of world building.&nbsp;

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:13.680
Hands down, simply a wonderful piece&nbsp;
of story telling. Thanks guys. Piece.

